                <pb facs="0134" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.1115A/871: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hare</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-12T18:00:00+02:00">June 12, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 12—3:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>102. <hi rendition="#italic">Excalibur</hi> is now in Alexandria.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Assuming vessel returns via Mediterranean should warning be given in
                        accordance with paragraph No. 2, Department’s telegram No. 37, May 16, to
                        Ankara.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>If vessel proceeds via Red Sea should similar warning be given.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>If Department’s authorization is required for validation of passports of
                        persons desiring to proceed to the United States through the new combat zone
                        as implied by Department’s 27, March 25, to Bern, blanket authorization is
                        requested covering passengers sailing from Egypt on <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Excalibur</hi>.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hare</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
